\section*{Vlasov–Maxwell regularity}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
\textit{Relativistic Vlasov--Maxwell regularity}: The paper claims global classical well-posedness of the relativistic Vlasov--Maxwell equations in three dimensions for a single particle species with arbitrary admissible smooth data of the specified finite-energy and particle-support class. Neither smallness nor symmetry is required.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Mathematical claim 1.} Let $u(v)=v/\sqrt{1+|v|^2}$, $\rho=\int f\,dv$, $j=\int u(v)f\,dv$. The system is \[\begin{aligned}\partial_tf+u\cdot\nabla_xf+(E+u\times B)\cdot\nabla_vf&=0,\\\partial_tE-\nabla\times B&=-j,&\partial_tB+\nabla\times E&=0,\\\nabla\cdot E&=\rho,&\nabla\cdot B&=0.\end{aligned}\] For arbitrary nonnegative $f_0\in C_c^\infty(\mathbb R_x^3\times\mathbb R_v^3)$ and $E_0,B_0\in C_b^\infty\cap L^2(\mathbb R^3;\mathbb R^3)$ satisfying the divergence constraints, the claim gives a unique global classical solution, smooth on every finite time interval, with compact phase-space support for $f$ on each such interval. Uniqueness refers to $C^1$ pointwise solutions with $E,B\in C([0,\infty);L^2(\mathbb R^3;\mathbb R^3))$ and one compact phase-space support set for $f$ over each bounded time interval. The data class $C_b^\infty$ requires every spatial derivative bounded. No smallness or symmetry is assumed, but compact support of the initial particle density is required.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
\textit{Relativistic Vlasov--Maxwell regularity}: The key quantity is the vector impulse integrated along a particle characteristic, with its norm taken after the integration. Retarded-field formulas, occupation estimates, and signed cancellation bound the time needed for successive momentum doublings. The lower bounds have divergent total length, so particle momentum support cannot blow up in finite time and the continuation criterion closes.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
\textit{Relativistic Vlasov--Maxwell regularity}: The system is relativistic Vlasov--Maxwell with a single species in three spatial dimensions. The admissible smooth data satisfy the stated finite-energy and particle-support requirements. Equality with a question that also permits other species conventions or nonrelativistic dynamics is not established here.

This page records partial support. Complete resolution of the catalogue question is not established by this record.

\subsection{Formal verification}
Family 362 describes Lean coverage for global smooth one-species relativistic Vlasov--Maxwell evolution for the stated admissible data class.

\textit{Relativistic Vlasov--Maxwell regularity}: The manuscript links \texttt{VlasovMaxwell.lean} (declaration \texttt{OAI.RVM.global\_classical\_solution}).

The documented selection includes this manuscript’s main assertion; that assertion retains the restrictions stated above.

This site has not run the Lean development. These links describe OpenAI’s selected formal statements and should be read with their stated scope.

